 - Tier: happy-dom (default). The spec requires DOM rendering; happy-dom is the cheapest tier that observes it.
 - Scantling for localStorage shape at `scantlings/todo-storage.json`.
 
+## Current voyage
+
+Acceptance suite (Cypress, real browser) reports 10 failures on the current code.
+All stem from two defects in `js/app.js` that the happy-dom harness cannot detect:
+
+**Defect 1 — DOM detachment (failures 1-4).**
+`render()` at line 72 does `todoList.innerHTML = ''` then rebuilds every `<li>` from
+scratch, destroying element identity. A real browser holding a reference sees the
+element detached. Fix: mutate existing `<li>` nodes in place (toggle class, update
+checkbox) instead of rebuilding.
+
+**Defect 2 — Edit input hidden (failures 5-10).**
+The dblclick handler (line 109) captures `li` in its closure. After `render()`
+rebuilds the list, `li.querySelector('.edit')` searches the OLD detached `<li>`,
+which lacks the `editing` class, so its `.edit` input has `display: none`. Fix:
+re-query the DOM for the new `.edit` input after `render()`.
+
+**Durable specs added:**
+- `features/todo-dom-fidelity.feature` — 2 `@conformance` scenarios that fail on
+  current code via source-level analysis
+- `features/support/conformance.js` — step definitions for source inspection
+- `watchbill.json` — ordered work for QM
+
+All 40 existing scenarios still pass. 2 `@conformance` scenarios fail red.
+
 ## Next
 
-Dispatch QM with `watchbill.json` targets when production code exists.
