+Feature: DOM fidelity in a real browser
+  As a user
+  I want the app to preserve DOM element identity across state changes
+  So that browser-based interactions (click, focus, visibility) work reliably
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: In-place DOM mutation for toggle
+
+  @conformance
+  Scenario: The render function mutates existing nodes instead of rebuilding the list
+    Given I inspect the app source
+    Then the "render" function does not clear the todo list with innerHTML
+    And the toggle handler toggles the "completed" class on the existing <li>
+    And the toggle-all handler toggles the "completed" class on each existing <li>
+
+  Rule: Edit input re-query after render
+
+  @conformance
+  Scenario: The dblclick handler re-queries the DOM for the edit input after render
+    Given I inspect the app source
+    Then the dblclick handler does not use the captured "li" variable after calling "render()"
+    And the dblclick handler queries the document for the new ".edit" input after render
